class QueueArray {
    private int[] arr;
    private int front;
    private int rear;
    private int capacity;

    public QueueArray(int size) {
        capacity = size;
        arr = new int[size];
        front = -1;
        rear = -1;
    }

    public void push(int x) {
        if (rear == capacity - 1) {
            return;
        }
        if (front == -1) {
            front = 0;
        }
        rear++;
        arr[rear] = x;
    }

    public int pop() {
        if (front == -1) {
            return -1;
        }
        int popped = arr[front];
        if (front == rear) {
            front = -1;
            rear = -1;
        } else {
            front++;
        }
        return popped;
    }
}
```

The QueueArray class utilizes a fixed-size array for efficient enqueue and dequeue operations. The `push` method adds elements to the rear, and `pop` removes elements from the front, maintaining O(1) time complexity. Empty queue conditions are handled by returning -1.

